Most useful columns / how they will be used  

• `date`: restrict data to July 2017 (values “20170701”‑“20170731”).  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX`: same purpose when the wildcard table name is used.  
• `fullVisitorId`: identifies each visitor – lets us know who bought a YouTube‑related item.  
• `hits` (REPEATED RECORD) → `item` (REPEATED RECORD): contains product‑level purchase data.  
    – `item.productName`: the name of the product (needed both to find YouTube items and to list the other products).  
    – `item.itemQuantity`: quantity purchased (used for the “total quantity” calculation).  
• (optionally) `item.transactionId`, `visitId`, `visitStartTime` – only for extra context or de‑duping, not strictly required in the final step.  

Typical conditions we will need  

• `_TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'` – July 2017 tables only.  
• `LOWER(item.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'` – to flag YouTube products.  
• `LOWER(item.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'` – to exclude such products in the final list.  
• `fullVisitorId IN ( … )` – to keep only visitors who bought at least one YouTube‑related product.  

Below are ten successive (different) exploratory‐to‑final SQL queries, each capped with `LIMIT 20`.  
(The project/dataset/table names are exactly as they appear in the public sample set.)

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at one July table: product names & quantities
SELECT
  date,
  fullVisitorId,
  itm.productName AS product_name,
  itm.itemQuantity AS quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170701`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show only rows whose product name mentions “YouTube”
SELECT
  fullVisitorId,
  itm.productName,
  itm.itemQuantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170705`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
WHERE LOWER(itm.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Distinct visitors that bought any YouTube product on 10 July 2017
SELECT DISTINCT
  fullVisitorId
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170710`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
WHERE LOWER(itm.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Any other (non‑YouTube) products those same visitors bought on 10 July
WITH yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170710`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
  WHERE LOWER(itm.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
)
SELECT
  s.fullVisitorId,
  itm.productName,
  itm.itemQuantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_20170710` AS s,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
WHERE s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
  AND LOWER(itm.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Aggregate: total quantity per product (all visitors, whole July)
SELECT
  itm.productName AS product_name,
  SUM(itm.itemQuantity) AS total_qty
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
GROUP BY product_name
ORDER BY total_qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Flag every visitor who bought at least one YouTube product in July
SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
  AND LOWER(itm.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Combine: product totals but only for those flagged visitors (still incl. YouTube)
WITH yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
    AND LOWER(itm.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
)
SELECT
  itm.productName AS product_name,
  SUM(itm.itemQuantity) AS total_qty
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
GROUP BY product_name
ORDER BY total_qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as 7, but explicitly excluding the YouTube products
WITH yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
    AND LOWER(itm.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
)
SELECT
  itm.productName AS product_name,
  SUM(itm.itemQuantity) AS total_qty
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
  AND LOWER(itm.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'
GROUP BY product_name
ORDER BY total_qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Bring the list down to only the top product (highest qty) – verification step
WITH yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
    AND LOWER(itm.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT
    itm.productName AS product_name,
    SUM(itm.itemQuantity) AS total_qty,
    RANK() OVER (ORDER BY SUM(itm.itemQuantity) DESC) AS rnk
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
    AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
    AND LOWER(itm.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'
  GROUP BY product_name
)
SELECT product_name, total_qty
FROM ranked
WHERE rnk = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final concise answer query – returns the distinct non‑YouTube product
--     with the highest total quantity among July‑2017 visitors who bought
--     any YouTube‑related product.
WITH yt_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
    AND LOWER(itm.productName) LIKE '%youtube%'
),
product_totals AS (
  SELECT
    itm.productName      AS product_name,
    SUM(itm.itemQuantity) AS total_qty
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
    AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM yt_buyers)
    AND LOWER(itm.productName) NOT LIKE '%youtube%'
  GROUP BY product_name
)
SELECT product_name, total_qty
FROM product_totals
ORDER BY total_qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Running query 10 will list the product(s) in descending order; the first row (rank 1) is the distinct product with the highest total quantity purchased by visitors who also bought at least one YouTube‑related item in July 2017.
